<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- G11a-2 fixture, written by hand for the parity harness of PPP (no source music): an outer repeat (three times) around an inner repeat with a first and a second ending. Bar 1 opens the outer repeat, bar 3 the inner one, bar 4 is the first ending (it closes the inner repeat), bar 5 the second ending, bar 6 closes the outer repeat (times=3), bars 7 and 8 follow. The order of the old player (kept, E4): 1 2 3 4 | 3 5 6 | 3 6 | 3 6 7 8 - a first ending whose repeat sign is skipped on the second time leaves the inner start on the stack, so the outer repeat of three goes back to bar 3, not to bar 1. -->
